(837100, 94767, 11800, '<td valign="top">Nice beadwork. I used to do that. <br/>The picture looks way overexposed possibly because of spot metering on the dark center. In a situation like this, I usually take a test shot with the camera metering and then manually adjust the time to get the proper exposure. I usually don''t mess with the f stop after I determine the amount of dof I want. On this one I would have shortened the time by 2 increments. Example: the auto setting said 1/60s I would have set it manually to 1/125s. Some people would bracket but I find doing it manually helps me have more precise control.</td>', 'Nice beadwork. I used to do that. The picture looks way overexposed possibly because of spot metering on the dark center. In a situation like this, I usually take a test shot with the camera metering and then manually adjust the time to get the proper exposure. I usually don''t mess with the f stop after I determine the amount of dof I want. On this one I would have shortened the time by 2 increments. Example: the auto setting said 1/60s I would have set it manually to 1/125s. Some people would bracket but I find doing it manually helps me have more precise control.', '2004-08-02 12:38:29.000000', NULL, 1),
