(850462, 95159, 24413, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone for your comments!  This was my first submission and I learned a lot from it.  This feather is from my Blue &amp; Gold Macaw.  So it is actually a blue feather to answer a couple of comments from people who didn''t see blue.</td>', 'Thanks everyone for your comments!  This was my first submission and I learned a lot from it.  This feather is from my Blue & Gold Macaw.  So it is actually a blue feather to answer a couple of comments from people who didn''t see blue.', '2004-08-09 08:49:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(850493, 95056, 19446, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone who voted this high and/or gave constructive comments.  I had a really bad case of photographer''s block and couldn''t come up with anything non-clice (sky, water...) then my son found the feather and say "how about this for the challenge?"  Figures an 11 year-old would be partly responsibile for my highest scoring entry.  And yes, I have thanked him!<br/> <br/>To answer some of the qustions posed during the challenge, the feather was naturally lit with difused light; the small aperture &amp; long shutter account for the richness in tones.  OK, OK, I should have known better than to post a photo w/ such a large frame - there''s almost always an active thread bashing boarders.  For thoes of you that didn''t like the "shadows" on the right... this is a Blue Jay''s freather and those are it''s natural markings.</td>', 'Thanks to everyone who voted this high and/or gave constructive comments.  I had a really bad case of photographer''s block and couldn''t come up with anything non-clice (sky, water...) then my son found the feather and say "how about this for the challenge?"  Figures an 11 year-old would be partly responsibile for my highest scoring entry.  And yes, I have thanked him! To answer some of the qustions posed during the challenge, the feather was naturally lit with difused light; the small aperture & long shutter account for the richness in tones.  OK, OK, I should have known better than to post a photo w/ such a large frame - there''s almost always an active thread bashing boarders.  For thoes of you that didn''t like the "shadows" on the right... this is a Blue Jay''s freather and those are it''s natural markings.', '2004-08-09 09:23:17.000000', NULL, 0),
