(852361, 94724, 19672, '<td valign="top">i really liked this one....<br/>(gave it a 9 or a 10 i believe)<br/> <br/>But I am really curious how people are doing these black and white photos but with a single object blue? i mean, I could do it with digital editing (mask the guitar and turn the rest b&amp;w)....was that allowed?<br/> <br/>*ponder*<br/> <br/>Or are people using a filter? I am very interested in this technique....</td>', 'i really liked this one....(gave it a 9 or a 10 i believe) But I am really curious how people are doing these black and white photos but with a single object blue? i mean, I could do it with digital editing (mask the guitar and turn the rest b&w)....was that allowed? *ponder* Or are people using a filter? I am very interested in this technique....', '2004-08-10 11:19:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(852388, 94878, 714, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by greslizzz:</b></div><hr/><i> It is amazing how different points of view people can have: what for me it is an artificial, forced and rigid composition (that is why I do not see it elegant), for others it is meaningful.<br/> <br/></i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/><b>RIGID</b> 1 a : deficient in or devoid of flexibility &lt;rigid price controls&gt; &lt;a rigid bar of metal&gt; b : appearing stiff and unyielding &lt;his face rigid with pain&gt;<br/> <br/>hmmm..she does not look rigid.  Look at her face.  She is doing this with ease.  No pain involved that I can see.</td>', 'Originally posted by greslizzz: It is amazing how different points of view people can have: what for me it is an artificial, forced and rigid composition (that is why I do not see it elegant), for others it is meaningful.   RIGID 1 a : deficient in or devoid of flexibility <rigid price controls> <a rigid bar of metal> b : appearing stiff and unyielding <his face rigid with pain> hmmm..she does not look rigid.  Look at her face.  She is doing this with ease.  No pain involved that I can see.', '2004-08-10 11:41:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(852392, 95001, 24885, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by dagaleaa:</b></div><hr/><i> very nice photo, but I am hard-pressed to find the blue......yet, I do like it! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yes... you are right.  No blue.  I need to read the challenge directions more carefully!  I redid the photo which can be seen in the "Latest Images" gallery at my website: www.fstopblues.com.  It has a deep blue tint in the sky... and is a better overall treatment of the photo.  Check it out if you like.  Thanks for your comment.</td>', 'Originally posted by dagaleaa: very nice photo, but I am hard-pressed to find the blue......yet, I do like it!   Yes... you are right.  No blue.  I need to read the challenge directions more carefully!  I redid the photo which can be seen in the "Latest Images" gallery at my website: www.fstopblues.com.  It has a deep blue tint in the sky... and is a better overall treatment of the photo.  Check it out if you like.  Thanks for your comment.', '2004-08-10 11:42:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(852393, 95001, 24885, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by dagaleaa:</b></div><hr/><i> very nice photo, but I am hard-pressed to find the blue......yet, I do like it! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for your comment.  See my previous one please.</td>', 'Originally posted by dagaleaa: very nice photo, but I am hard-pressed to find the blue......yet, I do like it!   Thanks for your comment.  See my previous one please.', '2004-08-10 11:43:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(852395, 95001, 24885, '<td valign="top">Yes... you all are right. No blue. I need to read the challenge directions more carefully! I redid the photo which can be seen in the "Latest Images" gallery at my website: www.fstopblues.com. It now has a deep blue tint in the sky... and is a better overall treatment of the photo. Check it out if you like. Thanks to all for your comments.</td>', 'Yes... you all are right. No blue. I need to read the challenge directions more carefully! I redid the photo which can be seen in the "Latest Images" gallery at my website: www.fstopblues.com. It now has a deep blue tint in the sky... and is a better overall treatment of the photo. Check it out if you like. Thanks to all for your comments.', '2004-08-10 11:45:26.000000', NULL, 0),
